00:01:00.578 --> 00:01:02.210
who work at the Smithsonian

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:05.730
or the National Archive,
and all that type of stuff.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:06.563
Yeah, right.

00:01:06.563 --> 00:01:09.567
But today we gotta tell you

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:14.523
about our expedition with our boys.

00:01:14.523 --> 00:01:15.630
Yeah, the camping trip.
When we went

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:16.930
to Death Valley.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:20.240
I, as you might have remembered,

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:23.919
in my top 10 moments of the year,

00:01:23.919 --> 00:01:26.153
I don't remember what number
it was, but it was up there,

00:01:26.153 --> 00:01:28.387
it was in the top 10 of my
favorite things that happened,

00:01:28.387 --> 00:01:31.278
was our trip that we took with the boys.

00:01:31.278 --> 00:01:33.351
Me and my boys.
I think it was number four.

00:01:33.351 --> 00:01:35.432
Maybe, me and my boys, Locke and Shepherd,

00:01:35.432 --> 00:01:37.450
you and your boys, what are their names,

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:38.283
Lincoln and Lando.

00:01:38.283 --> 00:01:39.443
I think their names are Lincoln and Lando.

00:01:39.443 --> 00:01:42.660
And to Death Valley.

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:45.090
And so we said we would
not talk about it at all

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:45.923
on that podcast

00:01:45.923 --> 00:01:49.915
because a number of stories were generated

00:01:49.915 --> 00:01:53.009
during our short trip,
that we will now share.

00:01:53.009 --> 00:01:54.312
I'm so glad that we did it,

00:01:54.312 --> 00:01:57.079
I gotta say it was my idea,

00:01:57.079 --> 00:02:00.010
I don't know if that's
true but I'm gonna say it,

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:01.530
it was my idea.

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.843
I was like, let's take the
boys on a camping trip.

00:02:03.843 --> 00:02:06.380
I don't recall, so I'll give you credit.

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:08.693
I was definitely looking
for another opportunity

00:02:08.693 --> 00:02:11.660
to rent a Sprinter van

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:15.284
and dabble, once again, in that #vanlife.

00:02:15.284 --> 00:02:19.600
So, that's been on my mind a lot

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:22.803
and Christy and I went, highlight of 2020.

00:02:23.705 --> 00:02:27.803
But yeah, I wanted to
give it a kid mode test.

00:02:27.803 --> 00:02:32.088
And I'd only used my, I call it my rig,

00:02:32.088 --> 00:02:32.921
is that what you would call my FJ Cruiser?

00:02:32.921 --> 00:02:34.654
Sure.

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:38.808
My FJ Cruiser, which I recently invested

00:02:38.808 --> 00:02:41.904
in some work being done on it.

00:02:41.904 --> 00:02:43.274
I got the rooftop tent,

00:02:43.274 --> 00:02:45.067
that was all for my solo trip.

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:47.140
But the thing that I
learned on my solo trip

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:52.140
is that I needed a more
efficient way to store things,

00:02:53.225 --> 00:02:56.657
especially if I was gonna
take any other beings with me

00:02:56.657 --> 00:02:59.151
on a camping trip.

00:02:59.151 --> 00:03:00.753
And I don't know if you noticed

00:03:00.753 --> 00:03:02.428
how proud I was of my drawer.

00:03:02.428 --> 00:03:04.398
I did notice how proud
you were of your drawer.

00:03:04.398 --> 00:03:05.878
Yeah, I got a drawer

00:03:05.878 --> 00:03:08.756
and you might think, what do
you mean you got a drawer?

00:03:08.756 --> 00:03:12.840
I got a drawer, a metal drawer, that,

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:16.050
if you look at an SUV, the back of an SUV,

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:18.550
you've got the part behind the back seats,

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:19.450
what would you call that?

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:24.450
The boot is what Christy
and her family call it,

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:26.139
but I always called the boot

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:28.169
the thing where your boots would go,

00:03:28.169 --> 00:03:29.928
where your feet go in
the front of the car,

00:03:29.928 --> 00:03:32.040
but I think I'm wrong, actually.

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:32.928
That doesn't make any sense.

00:03:32.928 --> 00:03:34.993
They call a trunk a boot.

00:03:34.993 --> 00:03:36.585
Well, it's not a trunk

00:03:36.585 --> 00:03:39.300
because it's just the back of an SUV.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:40.500
The back end.

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:44.140
There's a drawer that has been made,

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:46.780
a metal drawer, to fit the entire thing.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:49.959
And so, basically, it raises
the level of the floor up,

00:03:49.959 --> 00:03:51.695
so you still have all that space,

00:03:51.695 --> 00:03:54.095
but then there's a foot deep drawer

00:03:54.095 --> 00:03:56.465
that covers that whole thing.

00:03:56.465 --> 00:03:58.195
It's not cheap.

00:03:58.195 --> 00:03:59.250
It's not cheap.

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:00.350
Are you prepared to say how much you paid

00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:04.094
for one drawer to go in
the back of your truck?

00:04:04.094 --> 00:04:06.247
No, I'm not.

00:04:06.247 --> 00:04:08.483
It's a very expensive drawer.

00:04:09.623 --> 00:04:12.285
Less than $1,000.

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:13.704
Oh, okay.

00:04:13.704 --> 00:04:15.710
I actually thought it
was more than $1,000.

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:16.543
No.

00:04:16.543 --> 00:04:20.322
So, and by the way, I'm
sniffing 'cause of an allergy,

00:04:20.322 --> 00:04:23.113
I waited too long to take my pill today.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:28.506
I waited too long to take my pill today.

00:04:28.506 --> 00:04:31.082
I hate when I bring
allergies to "Ear Biscuits",

00:04:31.082 --> 00:04:33.214
but, every once in a while, I do.

00:04:33.214 --> 00:04:34.758
So anyway.

00:04:34.758 --> 00:04:36.210
If it makes your eyes water

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:37.509
it can look like you're getting emotional.

00:04:37.509 --> 00:04:42.509
This drawer, I was excited
about time with my sons,

00:04:43.441 --> 00:04:45.141
but I was most excited about the drawer.

00:04:45.141 --> 00:04:46.160
But pulling it out?

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:47.640
Over and over again.

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:48.473
Then pushing it back in.

00:04:48.473 --> 00:04:49.502
So smooth.

00:04:49.502 --> 00:04:53.231
But it's funny how just one
drawer, properly spaced,

00:04:53.231 --> 00:04:55.096
can change everything.

00:04:55.096 --> 00:04:56.260
Really, though?

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:57.093
Really?

00:04:57.093 --> 00:04:59.804
You didn't see how inefficiently
I had packed everything

00:04:59.804 --> 00:05:01.148
on my solo trip,

00:05:01.148 --> 00:05:02.427
because I didn't have to
worry about it too much.

00:05:02.427 --> 00:05:04.186
'Cause you gotta unpack the stuff

00:05:04.186 --> 00:05:05.848
